 6. 🕯️ Oregon teacher prevented more deaths 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Community members grieve at the site of a makeshift memorial in front of Silver Rail Elementary School in Bend, Ore. Photo: Mathieu Lewis-Rolland/Getty Images A teacher threw her phone at the teenage gunman who killed four people at an elementary school in Bend, Ore., then tackled and fought with him, likely saving lives before he was shot by a father who followed him into the building, police said yesterday.

 City of Bend Police Chief Mike Krantz called the teacher's actions "heroic" during a news conference and said she wasn't injured. He identified the attacker as 16-year-old Griffin J. John II and said all of the victims were shot in the same classroom. John was once a special needs student at Silver Rail Elementary, authorities said, and he attacked a classroom with special needs students. Read more. 

 
 
