 8. ⚖️ 1 for the road: Record-breaking pumpkin 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Frerich Farms Facebook page A 3,156-pound pumpkin  in Coventry, R.I., was certified by Guinness World Records as the largest pumpkin ever weighed.

 Ron Wallace's behemoth  crushed the previous record by nearly 300 pounds, becoming the first pumpkin to break the 3,000-pound barrier. He grew it inside a greenhouse, and there was "near-perfect" weather for much of the growing season, he told Guinness . Go deeper . 

 
 
